#====================================================================
# Draft knowledge entry - cohomcalg 0.32 CLI --help returns rc=1 (expected)
# Source package: cohomcalg/0.32
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-cohomcalg-0.32-cli-help-rc1-test
trigger_tool:           conan|test_package
phase:                  testing
error_signature:        --help failed|Error 1 while executing|test\(\) method

severity:               3
category:               testing|cli|smoke-test
match_keywords:         --help, --version, exit code 1, rc=1, smoke test, test_package, CLI tool, expected non-zero, main return 1, ParseCmdLineArguments, banner check, help gate, L2 smoke

title:                  CLI --help may legitimately exit 1; smoke test must check output, not rc, for help banners

root_cause:             >
    Legacy CLIs sometimes implement --help by printing the help text and returning
    non-zero from main (e.g. cohomcalg 0.32: ParseCmdLineArguments() returns false
    for --help, and main() does `return 1;`). This is upstream behaviour, not a
    defect. A test_package smoke test that gates on `cohomcalg --help && echo OK`
    (i.e. treats rc=0 as the pass condition) fails spuriously:
        [test] cohomcalg --help
        ❌ --help failed
        ConanException: Error 1 while executing
    The banner is printed correctly; only the exit code is 1.

affected_scope:         Any CLI tool whose --help path returns non-zero by design,
                        adapted with a test_package/conan L2 smoke test.

verification_cmd:       |
  cd <worktree> && conan create archives/c/cohomcalg/0.32 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 --build=missing --user=ohpcd --channel=stable

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           help-banner-content-check
rec_description: >
    In test.sh: run `"$BIN" --help > help.out 2>&1 || true` (tolerate rc), then
    `grep -Fq "cohomCalg v0.32" help.out` to assert the banner, and keep the real
    correctness gate on an actual computation (feed a sample input and assert the
    mathematical result + "Program run successfully completed"). Do not patch the
    upstream main() merely to make --help return 0.
rec_command:            |
  "$BIN" --help > help.out 2>&1 || true; grep -Fq "cohomCalg v0.32" help.out
rec_auto_fix:           true
rec_impl:               manual

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      patch-main-help-rc
fallback_description:   If the platform/CI gate strictly requires rc=0 for --help and
                        upstream refuses to change, a minimal main() patch adding
                        `if (help) return 0;` is possible but needs PR rationale (E503 precedent: jshn).
fallback_command:       (see E503 libubox jshn precedent)
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          patch

forbid_1_pattern:       ignoring rc entirely for the primary correctness test
forbid_1_reason:        Only the help-banner probe may ignore rc; the primary test must still
                        assert a real computation exit code 0 and output content.
forbid_1_consequence:   A broken binary could pass the smoke test (false green).

similar_to:             [E503, E357]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

